{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/134031-1001-geist-plot-hooks","id":134031,"title":"1001 Geist plot hooks!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-12T10:31:09-07:00","id":134031,"title":"1001 Geist plot hooks!","content":"Hey guys, I don't see one, so I figured I'd start a thread for this and see what pops up!<br /> <br /> Just to get us started:<br /> <br /> So, My Krewe was in the down below the other day and we stumbled onto a big fight going on. At first we thought it was some sort of warzone when we realized the guys fighting were other bound! They looked like they'd been down there for a while too... We skedaddled back to the surface, but not before I got a few pictures... they're all wearing insignias of some of the global krewes that are supposed to have existed in the 60's...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T12:05:08-07:00","id":134136,"title":"","content":"Ghosts starts disappearing all across town, with no discernable cause. After much research and many grueling nights, the Krewe finally track the cause of the disappearances to a mortal Necromancer. This Necromancer claims he is merely trying to help the shades depart a tormentet existance, useing a spell he has created, which he says sends them to the Abode of Shades, a place he calls Stygia. Can the Necromancer be trusted? What is this Stygia and is the Necromancer in his right to forceibly banish the shades, even if this &quot;Stygia&quot; is a better existance than the Twillight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1958,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","user":"Krobeles","date":". 05-12-2014, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T20:43:09-07:00","id":137653,"title":"","content":"A handful of interconnected ones:<br /> <br /> Practically overnight, sharp objects across town become Lightning-Struck Charms with relatively little provocation.<br /> <br /> The Knights of Damocles, an up-and-coming krewe, rise in prominence in a matter of weeks, growing to control most of the local assets on the strength of their bargains and the awful curses that befall those who betray them.<br /> <br /> The Kerberos known as Madam Guillotine has made all manner of overtures on the Knights' behalf, and in the moonlit skies above the city the unquiet dead say they can see the curve of a vast blade descending at an immortal's pace.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Roland, one of the successors of the Damocles channel, returns to town. He bears a heavily wrapped parcel that screams with poisonous entropy; word on the Twilight Network is sparse, but one thing manages to trickle through: the package was found on the banks of the River of Hate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-15-2014, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T09:31:05-07:00","id":138148,"title":"","content":"Unrelated posts on the Twilight Network are noting previously tranquil ghosts have turned hostile, seemingly overnight.<br /> Six cities in as many days with no connection between the Krewes.<br /> <br /> Following the cities on a map and starting with the first post, the cities are lining up to form an infinity symbol. Can Krewes<br /> in the next six cities figure out what's coming before the symbol is complete?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is just my bright, shiny two cents.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. I try not to argue in forums. It's like pouring concrete in a river. It doesn't get you anywhere in the short term and it poisons the environment long term.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2668-asmenedas","name":"Asmenedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2668_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T13:05:20-07:00","id":138343,"title":"","content":"The local community is spooked. The ghosts in the city - even the incoherent ones - seem to be humming a tune at 2am every night. Every night. In sync. It's not just weird either: it's getting louder by the night and no one is able to get a good nights rest because of it. Word on the TN is that the tune has been heard before - in an underworld Dominion nicknamed 'the unending wedding'<br /> <br /> Someone's dumped what looks like old circus equipment in a field outside of town. Local authorities are investigating during the day, but a couple of Krewes have decided to hold a flesh fair there tonight! Funny thing though, no one knows who went to the trouble of actually setting up the tents, fun houses and rides. <br /> <br /> Something's not right with the weather lately. Freak storms keep popping up overnight, seemingly centred around a park in the center of the city. People are going missing, and a few of them have come back - as incoherent ghosts muttering about biblical plagues - waves of locusts, a stream turning from water to blood, diseased animals and other crazy stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T20:21:20-07:00","id":201746,"title":"","content":"Something big is going down. Every one of the Bound in the nearby area has gained access to a key no one has heard of before, and that is almost addictive to use. Someone better figure out what's going on before things get ugly. <br /> <br /> Whelp, it was only a matter of time. One of the Bound has thrown his hat in the ring for the up coming Senate Elections, and he's not exactly being quiet about the whole &quot;set things on fire with my mind&quot; shtick. If you want to take him down, you better do it before even the Quick catch on to the fact it isn't CGI...(Twist: He's one of the Sancrosact, and plans to put as many resources as possible into wiping other Bound off the face of the Earth... Even if he has to start a war to do it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T13:25:59-07:00","id":202342,"title":"","content":"Somebody posts a map to the Pearly Gates on the Twilight Network. It's only six Rivers deep.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters are starting to be haunted by the ghosts of themselves.<br /> <br /> The Stricken have divided themselves into two factions. Half bearing Momentos and colours honouring the White Horseman. The other half dedicate themselves to King Rat, a mythological figure who served a similar role to the White Horseman during the Black Death. Nobody seems to know why, not even the Stricken themselves.<br /> <br /> Some brilliant Necromancer has managed to twist ghosts into a fortress. Then he started cutting anchors, starting from the west. It doesn't quite exist in both the sunlit lands and the Underworld, but it's close. He's already planning the next one, and this time he's not cutting anchors - he's going to have the west Pass On.<br /> <br /> Something big is coming from the bottom of the Underworld. It's the sort of event Sin-Eaters worldwide turn up to help fight it back, but the word is that this one is a Geist and all it wants is somebody to bargan with. <br /> <br /> Ghosts who had Passed On start turning up in the Underworld looking traumatised. You're not getting much out of them, but they all claim something attacked heaven (or valhalla, or the Elysum Fields)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-19-2014, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T14:29:56-07:00","id":202392,"title":"","content":"This is shamlessly ripped off from a book called Johannes Cabal the Detective. It's a great book that I just finished, and this story could work well for a group of Bound. I guess for mages or hunters too, but I like Geist lol<br /> <br /> There are rumors of a river, deep in the forest outside of the city. Where the river flows, nothing grows. Ghosts avoid the area and whisper the whole thing is cursed. The Krewe decised to investigate. When they get there, they realize that the river is flowing with unholy water. Following the river, they come to the source: a cave. Inside the cave the Krewe finds a group of mercenaries led buy a Bound. They seem intent on performing some sort of ritual. The inside of the cave is carved with strange, evil looking script. At the center of the cave is a deep lagoon, almost a cenote, and lying within is an ornate tomb. The lake is full of holy water, and when it flows over whatever evil lies beneath it is corrupted. The Bound and his/her mercenaries seem intent on corrupting the holy water and raising whatever is trapped at the bottom of the lagoon. If the Krewe can't stop them, a powerful sorceror of an unnamed bygone empire, eyes black as the Abyss, rises from the churning, bubbling, bloody waters. This is not good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T19:24:26-07:00","id":202556,"title":"","content":"Awefully clich\u00e9d, this one is, but here you are:<br /> <br /> At first, everyone was excited for the new exhibit at the museum, Bound and Mortal alike. For the Mortals, it was a quaint look at a bygone civilisation while for the Bound, it promised a queer look, into the ancient buried secrets of the ancient Pharaohs themselves. What should've been a joyous time for all, quickly turned sour, when the newspapers ran a story of a break-in at the museum. Only thing stolen was the mummified remains of King Sekhmet The Great. Strangest thing too. The sarkophagos almost seemed to have been split open <i>from the inside.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T10:55:43-07:00","id":203065,"title":"","content":"The Krewe isn't doing anything special but has traveled to a neighboring city or town to take care of a newly haunted house. Things seem to be going well when a black SUV shows up. The official seeming people inside (if questioned) claim to be investigating a dangerous gas leak, and have paperwork to back it up. If the Krewe just observes, the rival team starts unloading a bunch of strange looking devices, including a structure that resembles a gate. What to do?<br /> <br /> So, it's TFV trying to power up one of it's technological Avernian Gates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T17:17:19-07:00","id":205451,"title":"","content":"Bring the Orpheus Group in from oWoD and have them start stealing work from the krewe with their projection tech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T09:14:37-07:00","id":206199,"title":"","content":"The local Krewes have found a ceremony that allows them to form massive golems out of dead flesh and plasm at cenotes. They've taken to having events where two sin eaters will take control of these golems and duke it out for entertainment and to settle disputes - leading to an interestingly morbid new take on gladiator arenas. Problem is, a powerful Geist has snuck through and grabbed control of one mid fight and intends to take its revenge on one of the spectators... (Internet points to anyone who spots where I stole the idea from!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T07:11:41-07:00","id":208276,"title":"","content":"The Krewe begins finding bugs. Little, identical, caterpillar like things, throughout the house and town. The city seems to have a plague of them, but they quickly find that only the supernatural community can see them. Also: they're getting bigger, and it's getting harder to find plasm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T08:54:14-07:00","id":219129,"title":"","content":"I have always thought Grandmother from Orpheus, or the Malfeans, make excellent bad guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T12:05:35-07:00","id":230398,"title":"","content":"An estate sale is announced, auctioning off the property of a reclusive eccentric who left no heirs. Sin-eaters who hear the name recognize him as one of their own, and an infamous one at that.<br /> <br /> Decades ago, the sin-eater spent much of his time obsessively studying and mapping the underworld, and his knowledge of its geography and structure were reputed to be unmatched. The auction manifest hints at documents, charts, works of arts, antiques of unknown providence...it's a veritable treasure trove.<br /> <br /> Every krewe in town (and a few beyond) want a slice of the pie, and it's a mad dash to claim the prize by any means necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T08:44:39-07:00","id":231534,"title":"","content":"A Geist that appears to be millions of chicken in one entity has been attacking KFC resterunts. It would be amusing if it weren't for the wholesale slaughter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T16:45:47-07:00","id":232082,"title":"","content":"Madre de Dios! Es <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/dhVOb1A.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">el Pollo Diablo!</a><br /> <br /> \u00a1S\u00ed! \u00a1He dejado en libertad los prisioneros y ahora vengo por ti!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T20:07:41-07:00","id":265101,"title":"","content":"A serial killer is in town, the thing about him is that all his victims becomes Ghosts when they die. But that's not the only thing,a day before they die all victims gets a vision about the murderer and he would change into one of the characters Geist. What does as is anyone's guess as the Geist an't talking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T11:35:11-07:00","id":522131,"title":"","content":"To everyone else, the room seems hollow. It's filled to bursting with stuff, but even with all those boxes full of castoff possessions, the room seems empty, echoing with lost hopes and shattered dreams.<br /> <br /> To the Bound, its standing room only.<br /> <br /> Packed wall-to-wall with the shades of the dead, clinging desperately to whatever was nearby when they died. When they finally realize one of the many people who enter the room can actually see them, hear them, talk to them, the room is filled with pleading, asking, demanding ghosts, wanting their business resolved so they can move on, so they can leave this empty room and its crowded occupants behind.<br /> <br /> For this reason, even the most dedicated of Sin-Eaters think twice before entering a Homicide Department Evidence Room.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T17:04:12-07:00","id":522672,"title":"","content":"A local bound has died for the last time, and somebody crashes his funeral. Specifically, his ghost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T02:19:52-07:00","id":525303,"title":"","content":"It bears mention, that the works of H.P Lovecraft are filled with all sorts of nice storyhooks readily available for storytellers to implement, almost copy-paste.<br /> The Evil Clergyman, The Terrible Old Man, and The Case of Charles Dexter Ward are all fine stories of mortal Necromancers with whom the Sin-Eaters would likely take issue.<br /> Pickmans Model would pose a strange, yet relatively benign if exceedingly morbid, npc that might be interesting.<br /> In particular, the story Herbert West - The Reanimator posits not only the titular Herbert West himself, which could be an antagonist or tragic anti-hero depending on how you wish to portray him, but also the Tomb Legions which show up towards the end. They would certainly make for a fine antagonist group, led by the headless doctor with whom West shared his methods of reanimation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T10:54:12-07:00","id":525595,"title":"","content":"A strange geist is murdering children in their sleep. Survivors of its attacks mention nightmares about the geist.<br /> <br /> Some kind of Super Zombie is brutally murdering people. At first, one would think it's a slasher... But not even a Mask is this hard to put down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T16:03:43-07:00","id":526041,"title":"","content":"Doctors, the police, the city as a whole is baffled as bodies of the recently dead seem to be missing organs. A person dies of a heart attack and the morgue finds their liver missing. A murder victim is sans a lung. Three people who died in a fire are missing their hearts. There are no wounds, pre or post mortem, nor any sign of wound.<br /> <br /> An old well, long disused as anything but a quaint minor attraction, now seems to connect directly into one of the Rivers of the Underworld, allowing a certain amount of the River's content to be drawn up each night.<br /> <br /> A group of vampires want a tour of the local Underworld for their 'research' and are willing to pa handsomely.<br /> <br /> Part of the city is awoken each night a ghostly drag races tear through the quiet early morning streets.<br /> <br /> The city's twilight starts to heave as all animals within an area leave trange, twisted ghosts when they die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T07:28:40-07:00","id":533169,"title":"","content":"A biotech corporation has found out about Geister, and have been trying to capture one for experimentation, whether they're in a person or not.<br /> <br /> A strange zombie has been spotted on the edge of town. It was quickly dealt with, but when it died, some weird kind of ghost flew out and away. It looked like an owl made of smoke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 05-30-2015, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T08:47:02-07:00","id":538421,"title":"","content":"A new drug has hit the streets - they call it Dust, which dealers claim allows a person to undergo an out-of-body experience. When a mortal takes it, their body grows rigid and they seem to become truly dead - but from their body comes the ghosts, the shades of the person that died. When the drugs effects end, the ghost dissipates, and the individual returns. It's had an effect on the local street - overdoses always leave a ghost, stuck in a repetitive loop of the emotions they felt while taking the drug - the Sin-Eaters do not seem to be able to draw these ghosts back to sense with plasm, because they are already 'whole'. Long term effects are... unknown. But more to the point is when the characters go to a place where everyone's overdosed on this drug... and recognize that one of the individuals who've overdosed on the drug are another known Sin-Eater. Thing is, his ghost has been left as well, and his Geist is no where to be found - and the Sin-Eater is left in an eternal loop of the emotion he felt when taking the drug: absolute, maddening Horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T15:27:19-07:00","id":540075,"title":"","content":"From the Promethean forums, but think about how Sin-Eaters would react to finding one of these:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lackey Man Ren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/403822-share-your-custom-lineages?p=529548#post529548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm entertaining the idea of creating a Lineage similar to the Galateids. They'll be ceramic dolls made with human ashes mixed in with the clay. Not sure which humor (probably blood given the effects of Disquiet) or what kind of bestowment. Their Disquiet will be weird. Most people will not feel it as hard, but children will. Kids will actually want to play with the Promethean! Eventually they will want the Promethean all to themselves though, and start getting violent with other kids who also want to play. Parents of the children under effect of Disquiet become fearful for their kids, and then make their Disquiet rolls at some kind of penalty.<br /> <br /> There aren't any myths or folklore that lend themselves to something like this, are there? That's one of the big stumbling blocks, right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am immediately reminded off a novel I read about a year ago, <i>Doll Bones</i>, by Holly Black. More of a ghost story, by an author best known for work well suited to Changeling. (Both Lost and Dreaming.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T18:48:43-07:00","id":549570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/134031-1001-geist-plot-hooks?p=540075#post540075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the Promethean forums, but think about how Sin-Eaters would react to finding one of these:<br /> <br /> <br /> I am immediately reminded off a novel I read about a year ago, <i>Doll Bones</i>, by Holly Black. More of a ghost story, by an author best known for work well suited to Changeling. (Both Lost and Dreaming.)</div> </div> </div> </div>On a semi-related topic, I came up with a Geist-made Promethean in the vein of the ones found in Saturnine Night. He's basically a walking corpse who serves as an unwilling anchor for the ghost who once owned his body. He's not a very cheerful fellow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T16:29:48-07:00","id":552329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/134031-1001-geist-plot-hooks?p=549570#post549570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On a semi-related topic, I came up with a Geist-made Promethean in the vein of the ones found in Saturnine Night. He's basically a walking corpse who serves as an unwilling anchor for the ghost who once owned his body. He's not a very cheerful fellow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I've seen that write-up, good stuff!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T05:59:10-07:00","id":631082,"title":"","content":"Lately, the Autochthonous Depths are busy -- refugee camps are forming in the closest parts of the Underworld. Sin-Eaters are badgered the minute they cross the threshold. Venturing further into the Underworld turns up a strange scene: the great rivers of the Underworld are flooding. And not cyclically -- they keep flooding, overflowing their banks every, constantly, steadily. The further down the Sin-Eaters go, the worse it gets. Whole Dominions are absent population, save the Kerberoi, who pace at the borders, unable to leave.<br /> <br /> The grapevine comes alive with news of a geist, not bound to any Sin-Eaters, who calls himself Pontifactor. He is hiring mercenaries -- preferably ghosts and other hoary things of the Underworld, but anyone who will accept the pay he offers (ancient golden Iranian coins, Roman sestercii, Greek oboli, any ancient coins, really) can fight for him. He and his rag-tag army are hunting the psychopomps. When they kill one, Pontifactor consumes the psychopomp and then builds a bridge from the stone of the underworld and the vital essence of the psychopomp -- a bridge across the river that the psychopomp used to ferry people across. Word reaches the PCs that one of their allies amongst the ferrymen is the Pontifactor's next target.<br /> <br /> A lone Sin-Eater comes to town, selling something amazing -- artifacts of a bygone age which can increase Synergy. They are simple affairs, and incredibly easy to use. They are expensive however, and the vendor does not part with them easily. Once his price is paid, however, these strange feathers do precisely what they're advertised to do: they raise a Sin-Eater's Synergy by <i>three dots</i> (max 10). There's no immediate catch...key word 'immediate.' What do the PCs do with these feathers, if they decide to acquire them? Keep them for themselves? Use them on Sin-eaters who have lost their way? And what will they do when the feathers' former owner (a tremendous raptor known as 'Ma'at') comes looking for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7353-voragosolitude","name":"VoragoSolitude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7353_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T08:54:02-07:00","id":631242,"title":"","content":"Chthonians, the Never-born beasts of the Lower Mysteries, gain a semblance of coherency after devouring a ghost. Some ghosts took cues from this, and started cannibalizing other ghosts- coherency and power tend to be equal for ephemerals, after all. And yes, it worked. These cannibal ghosts, called Specters by some sin-eaters, continue to eat other ghosts, even other specters, to gain mystic power and new memories. Normally, the most powerful specters, the hive-mind of devouring and devoured ghosts called the Once-born, stalk the Lower Mysteries together with Chthonians. Too bad that someone or something summoned one of those things straight to your neighborhood. Time for the philosophically bickering krewes to unite and drive back the thing before it devours the Skinlands. <br /> <br /> A crazy yet powerful sin-eater with potent Ceremonies performed an experiment; he split a ghost off from a living guy, boosted its Rank to exalt it to geist-hood, then shoved the confused spirit back to the mortal. The result, for all purposes and outside observation, looks just like a normal sin-eater. Did this mad sorcerer just invent a way for sin-eaters to 'reproduce'? Is it legit? The original sin-eater got murdered by someone (or something), so something's certainly up......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5789-acanthus","name":"acanthus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T19:06:11-08:00","id":810907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>acanthus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/134031-1001-geist-plot-hooks?p=631242#post631242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chthonians, the Never-born beasts of the Lower Mysteries, gain a semblance of coherency after devouring a ghost. Some ghosts took cues from this, and started cannibalizing other ghosts- coherency and power tend to be equal for ephemerals, after all. And yes, it worked. These cannibal ghosts, called Specters by some sin-eaters, continue to eat other ghosts, even other specters, to gain mystic power and new memories. Normally, the most powerful specters, the hive-mind of devouring and devoured ghosts called the Once-born, stalk the Lower Mysteries together with Chthonians. Too bad that someone or something summoned one of those things straight to your neighborhood. Time for the philosophically bickering krewes to unite and drive back the thing before it devours the Skinlands.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a really great way to integrate some Wraith stuff into Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T19:31:12-08:00","id":810918,"title":"","content":"The Twilight Network is buzzing about a Geist re-emerging: the Cloaked Shepherd, once the leader of a cult who venerated the dead and those who could speak for them. She has a Bound in tow, a police man acting as her &quot;shepherd to the lambs&quot; and isn't afraid of using his Curse manifestation on those he deems to deserve to die while driving. Sin Eaters are his favorite targets, especially those who rising from accidents he already caused, and somehow he has yet to run out of plasm. Worse part is, the cult the Shepherd once led is starting to come back again...<br /> <br /> Ghost Trees are usually a pain to deal with, but they usually don't pop up overnight. Three have emerged in the last week across neighboring cities, and they're unusually active ones at that, with more popping up the more time goes on. It's getting to the point that Hunters are starting to emerge, ones who don't quite appreciate that fire won't be putting down this &quot;spectral weed&quot; any time soon. Is someone cultivating the trees? And why are they so violent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T05:28:59-08:00","id":811070,"title":"","content":"There's a killer on the loose. That wouldn't be anything particularly unusual for Sin-Eaters, except that the victims don't have any wounds. They're not even physically dead, they're just vegetables, their bodies ticking over. But they <i>are</i> dead. They have ghosts and those ghosts are like any other, save that none of them remember their killer. All they remember is being suddenly assaulted by their worst memories and then the world going black. On each of the corpses, though, is a note from the killer. They all say the same thing: 'remember them', followed by a strange symbol and a date and time of death. The media are calling the culprit 'The Memorialist'. In the Underworld, there are stirrings of ghosts. They all say that something came up a few weeks ago, a Geist which looked like a living memorial statue, gold copperplate writing on grey stone. And there's something else working its way up from the Lower Mysteries, something that feels the same as the Geist did, except immeasurably more powerful.<br /> <br /> Heavily inspired by The Memorial Key thread by The Sword Emperor","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 01-18-2016, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T09:24:06-08:00","id":811160,"title":"","content":"A krewe of Sin-Eaters has built something strange: Some kind of submarine, designed to stave off the effects of the Ocean of Fragments. They're looking for volunteers, but does it work? And what terrible things may swim those depths?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T17:59:29-08:00","id":815147,"title":"","content":"Your krewe is confronted by a group of vampire, they are asking for a guide into the Underworld. There looking for the recipe for something known Starlite. But what can be so important that they are willing to delve into hell itself to gain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T20:35:59-08:00","id":815211,"title":"","content":"Just as a Krewe open up an avernian gate, a group of werewolves come out, traumatized for having been trapped in the underworld for nearly a week. What caused them so much grief, who trapped them there and why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T00:13:42-08:00","id":817447,"title":"","content":"Krewe comes upon a strange structure inside the underworld. It seems like someone is pumping a river up to the living world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T00:17:18-08:00","id":817449,"title":"","content":"Gaists exploring some out of the way sections on the bank of the river (the one with life) come upon strange sights. Ghosts and even Kerberoy change, they grow, mutate and act different, some even appear to be pregnant. What is causing this and what new, strange creatures will soon be born?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T00:20:46-08:00","id":817450,"title":"","content":"Something is hunting Geists. Members of Krewe vanish one by one, not to be seen or heard on any side of shroud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T00:23:37-08:00","id":817452,"title":"","content":"A strange figure have appeared in the Underworld. A tall, shrouded spectre gliding through dominions and rivers unimpeded and vanishing any ghosts that touch him. Gaists refuse to go near the thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T03:07:29-08:00","id":841798,"title":"","content":"Something is moving in the Dead Dominions. Those Sin-Eaters who have seen it and returned say that it looks like a giant, thrice the height of a normal man with dozens of arms sprouting from his torso. In each had there flickers a tiny, blue flame. It moves from Dominion to Dominion, seemingly uncaring for the Old Laws or the Kerberoi. It steps over the Rivers with ease, ignoring the Ferrymen and their prices. Some say that they've seen it bend down occasionally and thrust one of its hands into a shade's chest. When it withdraws its hand, the flame is gone and now flickers in heart of the ghost, which follows the creature. It has an entire following of these ghost now. The thing is that the ghosts seem to have reclaimed themselves. They shed the grey robes of the Underworld and are clad in whatever clothes they died in. They are cognisant and act as though they died only minutes ago. They venerate it as something like a messiah and its followers have begun to spill into the mortal world, converting ghosts into new followers.<br /> Classically-minded Bound are calling it the Hekatonchire. Or Prometheus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 05-03-2016, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T08:35:35-08:00","id":841911,"title":"","content":"<b>58)</b> [GMC Cross-over] A rumor filters in through the Twilight Network of a complex that has appeared in the upper reaches of the Underworld. Said to be guarded by genuine freaking Angels, they say that the spirits of the dead will be tested inside, and those found worthy cleansed of their sins and taken to Heaven. Those ghosts who pass through the glowing doors inside never return.<br /> <br /> + (If you need to get the Krewe interested) At least, until some nightmarish horror confronts the Krewe one evening. It says through a half-dozen voices that &quot;they&quot; went through the doors and experienced not Heaven, but a Hell of blood, gears, and blades, which cut and assembled them into the composite beast before you. &quot;They&quot; want vengeance for this deception and betrayal, and want the Krewe to find some way to separate them into their component ghosts again. <hr /><br /> <b>59)</b> [Optional Mage and/or Demon Cross-over] The Krewe starts encountering something wierd, even by their standards - people possessed or Claimed by <i>their own ghosts</i>. When questioned, they all admit to some missing time, but don't remember anything odd beyond that. They all suffered these blackouts in the general vicinity of the old manor just outside the Krewe's territory that was purchased recently. <hr /><br /> <b>60)</b> The Krewe investigate/pass-through the semi-infamous ghost town nearby. Everything seems fine until someone accidentally cuts themselves on a piece of debris. The spilled blood triggers some sort of curse and drags the whole town (and everyone in it) into the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-06-2017, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T08:19:02-07:00","id":880991,"title":"","content":"[Promethean crossover]<br /> A being has appeared in the Autocthonous Depths, something like an angel with wings of white fire. It wanders seemingly at random through the Underworld, never going deeper than the first River. It seems to choose ghosts by criteria known only to it, speaking to them of a 'divine fire' and giving each of them a flame from its wings, a tiny ember burning white. The flame even warms the dead and the ghosts gifted with the embers have become central to the communities of the dead, lighting fires which can stave off the numbing coldness of the Great Black.<br /> The fire can refine and change the cursed plasm of the Underworld, allowing the ghosts which live there to build new things. First camps, them houses and now townships are beginning to be built. The Gifted (as they are calling themselves) have become combination leaders, messiahs and high priests, commanding legions of architects, builders and constructors, ghosts who have idled, purposeless, for decades are finally being granted a purpose.<br /> However, with the rise of the civilization of the dead come the same problems that torment their living counterparts: greed, lust for power, envy. And, more worryingly for the Bound, many of them nurture a hatred for the self-proclaimed guardians of the gateway into the Great Beneath. A hatred which is now being heard by more ghosts than ever before. The Underworld is turning against the Sin-Eaters and the flames of the so-called Prometheus are spreading. Soon the world of the dead will be irrevocably changed. Will you help it along and try to reconcile with the kingdoms arising in the Underworld or will you attempt to nip this in the bud, extinguishing the all-too fragile flames of the nascent Kingdoms of the Dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T05:23:08-07:00","id":1094841,"title":"","content":"Rise!<br /> <br /> (Not my idea, but something from the Ascension forum's Plot Hooks, brought to us by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1067534-1000-mage-plots?p=1094794#post1094794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">27) On the internet, a series of bots post across message boards and social media, asking the same question: Have you see the disembodied head, with white hair, blue eyes, and a scar across his nose?<br /> <br /> No one knows who started this campaign, and most are quick to write it off as a bit of viral marketing, an ARG, or a meme no one gets the reference to. It flares into popularity as folks talk about it, making theories or parodies. Eventually, the meme fades into the background. No one had much to go on anyway, so it didn't have anywhere to grow. The bots just kept spamming their message, or variants on the message, and people learned to block or ignore them.<br /> <br /> Then, a few months later, a few of the dedicated or lucky users began noticing something. In one city, buildings were tagged with messages akin to the meme. Except the messages verifiably date from before the first appearance of the bots. In other cities and towns across the world, people began noticing certain individuals who ask around for the blue eyed severed head. They turn over every leaf they can, asking the police, criminal groups, the homeless, journalists, and random citizens if they've seen it. In one place, a detailed drawing of an elderly man's head - complete with white hair and beard - begins to circulate, handed out by a wandering street artist.<br /> <br /> At one point, law enforcement in a city in Saudi Arabia take issue with someone asking after people's severed heads (that the man was looking for a specific head was not relayed to them it seems), so they arrested him. They got him as far as the police station. They were found hours later, the station trashed, their heads cut off and placed in their hands. The same question - &quot;Have you seen the severed head with the blue eyes and white hair?&quot; - was scrawled on the station house walls, while another wall had a man-sized escape hole melted through it.<br /> <br /> Now, someone who apparently holds up this crusade has appeared in the PCs' own town, asking around for the now notable lost head. And like many of his ilk, he has a scar around his neck, and more than a little personal power.<br /> <br /> <br /> [The truth is that the head belongs to a Dullahan, an umbrood that appears as a headless knight. He appears to those who suffer from accidents or violence, and suffer decapitation. As their brains rapidly die, they are pulled into a misty realm, where the horseman appears and picks up their heads. He plants them atop his neck stump, and speaks to them through their own mouths. Tells them that he lost his own head, and wants it back. If the person agrees to look for it, the Dullahan will not only restore the person's head to its proper perch, but grant them supernatural gifts. Naturally, it's not really a choice at all, and many have taken the deal.<br /> <br /> The Seekers of the Head are not Infernalists, though they receive Investments after a fashion. The Headless Knight has no interest in souls or promoting suffering. He only wants one thing: his head. It's lost somewhere in the material world, and he needs agents to find it. The agents receive a bit of power in the bargain, which can include dots in Sorcery Paths - sometimes even Spheres, should the encounter with the Dullahan trigger an Awakening. All they must give in return is their quest. The Headless Knight hounds their dreams and assaults them with hallucinations, if they aren't actively looking for the head. The one who finds it is promised a rich reward. If they shirk their duties too much, however...well, the Dullahan is quick to remind them that he gave them renewed life. He can take it away, if he so chose. He's not running a charity.]</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T06:19:41-07:00","id":1094852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/134031-1001-geist-plot-hooks?p=1094841#post1094841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rise!<br /> <br /> (Not my idea, but something from the Ascension forum's Plot Hooks, brought to us by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> )<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bthis is very good. does he have any other plot ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T06:51:59-07:00","id":1094855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/134031-1001-geist-plot-hooks?p=1094852#post1094852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> \u200bthis is very good. does he have any other plot ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps? His various posts are centered on Ascension, so they're usually fit for Awakening, but the one I quoted up there just screamed Geist to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T15:07:36-07:00","id":1094955,"title":"","content":"<b>63)</b> Something has been drawing the Bereft to it, offering salvation. It's an Angel/Exile filling the gap with other Angels or Imperatives.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>64)</b> A Geist claiming to be from the future is offering new Keys (or just &quot;updating&quot; the Industrial key to have no Anachrontech penalties with even cutting edge tech).<br /> <br /> <b>65)</b> The Krewe encounters a procession of lantern-bearing ghosts - whose flames reek of the Divine Fire.<br /> <br /> <b>66)</b> You encounter a dog/cat/animal... With a Geist. An animal Sin-Eater. <i>How</i> did a non-sentient creature make the Bargain?<br /> <br /> <b>67)</b> Another Sin-Eater has discovered a method of negating the Synergy loss caused by dying and is teaching it to others. Then they end up murdered by the amalgamated ghosts of those who died in their place. And at least some of your Krewe learned their methods and employed them...<br /> <br /> <b>68)</b> Mediums are whispering about something (they don't know what, they can just <i>feel it</i>) coming. Spirits in the Shadow are going absent, starved of Essence. Those with connections to the Astral speak of a whole realm forming... or reforming. Ghosts have been behaving abnormally, engaging in rituals they never have before. It's as if they've converted to some strange cult. An occultist comes to the Krewe with what they think is the answer: Even dead Gods dream... especially when they are close to Waking Up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-06-2017, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T01:45:14-07:00","id":1382471,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure the number is right, but I'm gonna keep it going for some semblance of order.<br /> <br /> 69) Your favourite grandparent died last month.<br /> They died again a fortnight ago. And again two days ago. It happened yet again this morning.<br /> You're not sad that they're managing to avoid staying dead (after all, they are your favourite grandparent), but why &amp; how is this happening? You know they haven't become a Bound/sin-eater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T01:45:44-07:00","id":1382472,"title":"","content":"70) A colleague has been acting weird(er than normal).<br /> When investigating you discover that they have become possessed by a set of Old Laws &amp; are starting to turn into a kerberoi.<br /> You've never heard of anything like this happening before, so you have absolutely no idea what to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T01:47:07-07:00","id":1382473,"title":"","content":"Heads up: trigger warnings on this one.<br /> <br /> 71) There has been a sudden spike in suicides recently, with every suicide producing a ghost.<br /> This spike coincided with the local history museum getting a new artefact to show off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T01:48:02-07:00","id":1382474,"title":"","content":"72) A small area (rural town, small neighborhood, etc.) has started to overlap with a Dead Dominion.<br /> Note: I imagine the living place &amp; the Dead Dominion as being roughly the same size.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T01:48:39-07:00","id":1382475,"title":"","content":"73) Ghosts in the area are showing signs of being stronger than they used to be. And the ghosts are still growing in strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T01:49:25-07:00","id":1382476,"title":"","content":"74) There's a mass Native American grave in the area. From this mass grave rises a &quot;conglomerate ghost&quot; made from the souls of every Native American in that grave. They rise to take revenge on the white man.<br /> Note: as they have risen to take revenge on the white man, they specifically target white people. Anyone not white is ignored if possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T01:50:02-07:00","id":1382477,"title":"","content":"75) A powerful geist is bound to a whole krewe of sin-eaters. The krewe work in concert towards disturbing goals that make little sense to other sin-eaters.<br /> They claim that they are working towards fixing the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T01:50:38-07:00","id":1382478,"title":"","content":"76) One of the Rivers of the Underworld has started appearing in the living world. Not just the waters of the River, the actual River itself.<br /> Ghost activity where this River has started appearing has skyrocketed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T15:46:11-07:00","id":1393707,"title":"","content":"77) A posse of Reapers has been spotted around a hospital that had had a sudden rash of DOA cases. When confronted by the Krewe it\u2019s revealed that these Reapers aren\u2019t collecting the ghosts of these unfortunate souls but destroying them, lest the strange infection carried by these specters spread to others. The sin-eaters are caught in a dilemma: do they help the Reapers try to contain this Contagion, or do they attempt to free the ghosts and attempt to cure them their own way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T16:49:35-07:00","id":1399426,"title":"","content":"78.<b>The Labyrinth</b><br /> Labyrinths were used in the Eluesiniam Mysteries for centuries throughout Greece, used in rites only barely understand by modern archaeology.<br /> <br /> Several of these labyrinths are of no occult value, but a very rare few of them are Avernian Gates guarded by geists millennia old, older even than the Greeks who built the material world side of the labyrinth. Many of these geists are swollen, obese monsters, strange amalgams of ghost and wild beast, rendered feral and mute over the creeping passage of eons.<br /> <br /> But one labyrinth, as yet known only to Greek Sin-Eaters, is more than just an Avernian Gate, as it opens to a grim place of death somehow both Resonant with and yet distinct from the Underworld. In this strange pocket reality, the labyrinth goes much deeper into the earth. Mute shades herein hunger for blood, and burn in the touch of the sun, but are somehow neither vampires or ghosts.<br /> <br /> If you feed the shades blood, they can briefly speak, and what tales they tell! If fed enough blood, the shades'll teveal the existence of s heavenly graveyard. Here, the corpses of gods and mem alike lie side by side in repose. The shades claim the labyrinth once led to this necropolis, this &quot;Stygia&quot;, but that the way is now lost...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 06-27-2020, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T10:59:42-07:00","id":1463120,"title":"","content":"79.<b>Behemoth</b><br /> Crawling out of a world-famous Avernian Gate in [Fill-In-The-Blank] is a ghost so titanic it is too heavy to even crawl, forcing it to drag itself across the Twilight earth, face buried in the dirt. This massive spirit, a skinless horror of epic proportions, is slowly inchworming it\u2019s way towards a nearby city.<br /> <br /> What will it do when it gets there? How can it be stopped?<br /> <br /> Note:<br /> And yes, this story idea <i>is</i> blatantly stolen from Attack on Titan!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T14:18:58-07:00","id":1463156,"title":"","content":"80) <b>Deal With a <i>What?!</i></b><br /> <br /> Rumours have started spreading of a Sin-Eater who somehow managed to forge the Bargain with a <i>Cthonian</i> of all things. Naturally, most Bound brush it off as it just being the result of someone having had some bad cheese before going to bed, or whatever. That is until said Bound shows up in [Insert-Player-Home-Settlement], announces themselves and unintentionally sets every Geist in the Region into a fear-fueled, berserker-like frenzy in the process","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-17T16:52:21-07:00","id":1479038,"title":"","content":"81. <i>Some Truce With the Furies</i><br /> <br /> On a poorly understood schedule, or perhaps for the first time, several Avernian Gates open in synchrony around the area. From their depths billows a thick fog, borne from the Ocean of Fragments itself. Long-term exposure to the lingering mist causes memory and even identity loss, as a wanderer's sense of self spills out from them, leaving those caught in the fog's wake filled with lacuna, missing key aspects of themselves. Some of these lost fragments coalesce into ghosts in their own right, haunting the people and places for whom they are still important despite the amnesia.<br /> <br /> What is happening? Why is it happening? Is this the result of a Ceremony gone wrong (or right)? The machinations of a Chthonic God and its Reaper servants? Something even stranger? How can it be stopped? And if not stopped, how can it be harnessed to the Krewe's own ends?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T09:56:50-07:00","id":1487396,"title":"","content":"82)Something metaphysically <i>massive</i> moves through the layers of the Underworld, a ghost with strange Chthonian qualities, that resembles a humongous wolf-carcass animated by a vast ocean of maggots, beetles and other carrion-eaters. To behold it is lose one\u2019s sanity, as its mind bears down an unlucky interlopers with crushing force.<br /> <br /> It is not a ghost of a human or an animal, but of a <i>god</i>, something from the Stone Age that has grown in power, til it reattained godhood in the Underworld. It wants <i>out</i> of the Underworld to chase some sort of ancient adversary, but it cannot squeeze through any existing Avernian Gates.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eater krewes are being subborned by this horrible thing and the Reapers it has bound against their wills into its service. The PCs\u2019 krewe is next on the list of krewes to be subverted. Wat do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 07-21-2022, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T09:28:29-07:00","id":1487605,"title":"","content":"83)The PCs\u2019 krewe are invited to a grand gala thrown by Sin-Eaters, of Sin-Eaters, for Sin-Eaters. Reasonably mentally coherent ghosts serve as staff, and prizes will be handed out. (Most of these prizes are perfectly mundane, with a few Mementos thrown in here and there.)<br /> <br /> Then a mixed strike team of Necromancers and Abmortals armed with military-grade firearms and wearing tactical gear crash the party! They want everyone here, for a variety of gruesome Necromantic reasons!<br /> <br /> Wat do?<br /> <br /> 84)At a ruined casino in a Nevada ghost town (pardon the pun), one of the slot machines, somehow still functional, has acquired the power to alter fate of ghosts, Sin-Eaters, Moros mages and other supernatural beings deeply connected to the Underworld. One can only win twice, but one can <i>certainly</i> keep losing.<br /> <br /> Winning a round gives you a Beat to use on Underworld-related things, such as magic, certain Merits and so on.<br /> <br /> Losing, however, gives you the Hunted Condition, as the casino manager\u2019s ghost rises to make your day as miserable as possible.<br /> <br /> But losing twice or more gives you the Open Condition to a single ghost each time, starting with the casino\u2019s owner, and getting worse with each additional loss.<br /> <br /> 85)\u201dClaimed by the Dead is still Claimed.\u201d A Storm Lords-only pack is hunting Sin-Eaters, and they have the PCs\u2019 krewe in their sights.<br /> <br /> Wat do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 07-23-2022, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T20:22:02-07:00","id":1511041,"title":"","content":"86) Ghosts have started turning up in the Hisil. Why? What can be done for them?<br /> <br /> 87) A ghost with bizarre biomechanical body modifications shows up in the PCs town seeking entry into the Underworld, but none of the Avernian Gates will permit it to pass through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}